tendance, and workforce productivity; and locks, locksets, portable locks, and key systems. It also provides services and software, such as inspection, maintenance, and repair services for its automatic entrance solutions; software as a service, including access control, platform integration, and workforce management solutions; and ongoing aftermarket services, and design and installation offerings. In addition, the company sells its products and solutions to end-users in commercial, institutional, and residential facilities, including education, healthcare, government, hospitality, retail, commercial office, and single and multi-family residential markets under the CISA, Interflex, LCN, Schlage, SimonsVoss, and Von Duprin brands. It sells its products and solutions through distribution and retail channels, such as specialty distribution, e-commerce, and wholesalers, as well as through various retail channels comprising do-it-yourself home improvement centers, online and e-commerce platforms, and small specialty showroom outlets. Allegion plc was incorporated in 2013 and is based in Dublin, Ireland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John H. Stone | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $306K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $52K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Allegion plc is a large-cap industrials business with a $15.8B market cap on $4.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $686M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.22\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 8.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.050459149862728245},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (89% sell ratio, net $3.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (37% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Allegion (ALLE) is a Top-Ranked Momentum Stock: Should You Buy?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3021808/allegion-alle-is-a-top-ranked-momentum-stock-should-you-buy?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_momentum_score-3021808","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793713802.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Raised Guidance At Allegion (ALLE) Has Changed Its Investment Story","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-alle/allegion/news/how-raised-guidance-at-allegion-alle-has-changed-its-investm","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793579433.305,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Allegion (ALLE) Lifts 2026 Outlook Following Q3 Results As Valuation Questions Linger","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-alle/allegion/news/allegion-alle-lifts-2026-outlook-following-q3-results-as-val","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793457579.097,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.932,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]