alised volatility of 30% and a beta of 0.84, it moves roughly with the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.05 vs 5y 0.81), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $165.0M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 43% in the 2020 crash and 32% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $179 (margin of safety -3%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 11%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $136 to $239 (P10-P90).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 28% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 4.3% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.9% (vs the 8% bar).","The 11 covering analysts target $194 on average, 4% above the price.","The price implies 8.6% annual cash-flow growth."],"prof":["ROIC of 23% clears the cost of capital of 8.5% by 14pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have been steady (CV 0.12).","It converts 17% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.22x.","ROE of 31% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.5x equity multiplier).","It spends 3.2% of revenue on R&D and 0.7% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.6x net debt to EBITDA ($356.2M of cash against $2.0B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 8.5x.","Goodwill makes up 37% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 7.5% over 3 years, 8.4% over 5 years and 7.0% over 10 years.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 9.1% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.8x depreciation (2.4% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 25, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","Analysts expect 11.5% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.2%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 8 sales over the past year, net $3.8M sold.","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.6% (0.5% in buybacks and 1.2% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 0.9% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 12 consecutive years, raising it 8.4% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 13,300 employees, each generates about $306K of revenue, 0.8x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 6.1% a year.","That works out to $52K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.1M (10x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":68,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $152.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 53, gates 15/25)","ROIC 22.8% vs WACC 8.5%","FCF margin 16.9%","Revenue grew 8.4%/yr over 5y","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["Trades 3% above fair value of $179"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":152.43,"vc":{"base":179.33,"base_src":"dcf","bear":136.14,"bull":239.06,"alt_median":146.48,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.2243,"dispersion":0.1083,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"ALLE","date":"2026-11-06"}